>>>>> "Thierry" =3D=3D Thierry Bouche <Thierry.Bouche@UJF-GRENOBLE.FR> =
writes:

    > =BB My suggestion is to put a begin-page-hook to the output =
routine.
    > aren't page styles precisely this?

It should be independent of the page style.

    > I thought latex2e user interface was more or less frozen, maybe
    > your query should be taken into consideration for the
    > architecture of latex2e* page templates?

In my opinion something like \AtBeginPage should exist and it might be
used by the templates if desired. It is always better to have a hook
than to patch existing code.

If there would be something like \AtEndPage, the \afterpage package
would be much smaller, its code easier to understand and much easier
to maintain.

Reinhard

